    "cost_closing_html":  "About \u003cstrong\u003e$2.03 a bowl\u003c/strong\u003e. Canned tomatoes and rice keep the base almost free, so nearly every dollar in this pot went to the turkey where it belongs.",
    "shop_smart":  [
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eGreen bell peppers are the cheap ones.\u003c/strong\u003e Red, yellow and orange peppers are the same vegetable further along and they cost two or three times as much. Green is the right call here.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eCanned diced tomatoes and tomato sauce are the base.\u003c/strong\u003e Buy them by the case when they hit a sale price. They keep for years and they show up in half the recipes on this site.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eRice from the warehouse bag costs almost nothing per serving.\u003c/strong\u003e That is why it is the carb in so many of these builds. One bag covers this batch and a dozen more.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eWorcestershire is the secret in this pot.\u003c/strong\u003e One bottle lasts a very long time and it is what makes a tomato and turkey soup taste like it simmered all day."
                   ],
    "make_it":  [
                    "Weigh your empty mixing pot and write the number down for portioning later.",
                    "Cook the rice separately per the package and set it aside. Cooking it in the soup turns the whole pot to mush by day three.",
                    "Brown the ground turkey in the olive oil in your big pot over medium-high heat, breaking it up as it goes, until no pink is left.",
                    "Add the diced onion and the chopped green bell peppers and cook until they soften, then stir in the garlic for the last minute.",
                    "Pour in the beef broth, the diced tomatoes with their juice, the tomato sauce and the Worcestershire sauce.",
                    "Add the bay leaves, dried oregano and dried thyme, bring it to a simmer, and let it go for 25 to 30 minutes so the peppers go tender and the flavors settle.",
                    "Fish out the bay leaves, season with salt and black pepper, and stir the grated parmesan in off the heat."
                ],
